then McCarl city youth council has  existed since 1998 the youth council is  a group of youth aged 12 and 24 who act  as advocates for all young people in  Invercargill the youth council ensure  that young people's voices get heard by  the council and provides a youth  perspective on the council's decision  making here on the youth council we aim  to help organize events and projects  involving young people having a public  voice find create and push for things  for young people to do look at ways to  improve the social and physical  environment I want to help participate  in setting up things for youth to do and  the holidays after school things like  that youth organisations youth based  organizations cafes gaming lenders  things like that dream um pouco goes to  the youth council has been a fantastic  opportunity for me to involve myself in  making Invercargill more aware of issues  for young people and sleeping up to make  a difference in our community youth  council meets fortnightly on wednesdays  from 4pm to 530 p.m. during the school  term on the youth council we are offered  the opportunity to be involved in many  activities including attending trainings  and meetings passing information onto  our networks like our schools be  involved in representing and the cargo  at youth activities around the country I  joined the youth council was one of the  local nominees I was nominated by a  friend of mine down at the social  services and they told me to come along  and make a difference here in  Invercargill I was hoping to create more  fun activities for youth to do in this  bed time because I hear of a lot of  youth just sitting around playing  PlayStation the Youth Council consists  of up to 25 members to be a member you  will need to be between 12 to 24 years  of age live an or attend school training  or be employed within the Invercargill  city council area have the ability to  work with other people and work in a  team be proactive be committed to  attending meetings regularly be  nominated by your school or a youth  organization or you can volunteer to be  a member we aim to have as broad  possible group of young people  representing me appears and under cargo  it's been a great experience being on  the Youth Council I gained a social  conscience confidence in public speaking  I learned proper meetings procedure and  make some great new friends more sense  of lift I've managed to get a job as a  trainee accountant at a local accounting  firm and i'm currently sitting on a  community panel which i don't think i  would have been able to do without being  a part of the council to be selected for  youth council it's simple the call for  nominations or applications for youth  council members will be made in  august-september each year for the  following year secondary schools within  the city are invited to nominate two  members representing each school  applications for additional members will  be sought by public advertising and  promotion youth counselors will be  selected on their ability to demonstrate  leadership advocacy governance and  service skills for more information you  can see the youth council webpage on the  council website also keep up to date  with what the youth council is up to on  the Facebook page
 

